        "original_id": "7355eb73-631d-56c2-ab7b-a77d683b9e83",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Claude Simon, Paul Auster, Alain Robbe-Grillet, Alain Resnais, Nathalie Sarraute, Michel Butor\n- Movements: Nouveau Roman\n- Works: Last Year at Marienbad\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n\nFacts:\n- Claude Simon was born on 10 October 1913 and died on 6 July 2005.\n- Claude Simon was a French novelist and critic.\n- Last Year at Marienbad is a 1961 French-Italian film.\n- Last Year at Marienbad was released in the United States as Last Year at Marienbad and in the United Kingdom as Last Year in Marienbad.\n- Alain Robbe-Grillet was one of the figures most associated with the Nouveau Roman trend of the 1960s, along with Nathalie Sarraute, Michel Butor, and Claude Simon.\n- Last Year at Marienbad was directed by Alain Resnais from a screenplay by Alain Robbe-Grillet.\n- Paul Auster was born on February 3, 1947.\n- Paul Auster is an American writer and director whose writing blends absurdism, existentialism, crime fiction, and the search for identity and personal meaning.\n- Claude Simon received the 1985 Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- Paul Auster's books have been translated into more than forty languages.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
