        "text": "Page: Claude Simon. Sentence: Claude Simon (] ; 10 October 1913 – 6 July 2005) was a French novelist and critic, and the 1985 Nobel Laureate in Literature.\nPage: Paul Auster. Sentence: Paul Benjamin Auster (born February 3, 1947) is an American writer and director whose writing blends absurdism, existentialism, crime fiction, and the search for identity and personal meaning.\nPage: Paul Auster. Sentence: His books have been translated into more than forty languages.\nPage: Alain Robbe-Grillet. Sentence: He was one of the figures most associated with the \"Nouveau Roman\" (new novel) trend of the 1960s, along with Nathalie Sarraute, Michel Butor and Claude Simon.\nPage: Last Year at Marienbad. Sentence: L'Année dernière à Marienbad (released in the US as Last Year at Marienbad and in the UK as Last Year in Marienbad) is a 1961 French-Italian film directed by Alain Resnais from a screenplay by Alain Robbe-Grillet.",
